<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Clustering works by using the built-in cluster module in Node.js. This module allows you to create a master process that manages a cluster of worker processes. The master process listens for incoming requests and distributes them to the worker processes in a round-robin fashion. Each worker process runs a copy of your application code and handles incoming requests independently.)
/E (Clustering works by using the built-in cluster module in Node.js. This module allows you to create a master process that manages a cluster of worker processes. The master process listens for incoming requests and distributes them to the worker processes in a round-robin fashion. Each worker process runs a copy of your application code and handles incoming requests independently.)
